[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: the parser reads dates month first. That is
true for most of its reports. It is not true for all of them. Counted by cause, the reports fall
into three problems, and each has its own ticket in
[grzegorzp-commits/kb-4471](https://github.com/grzegorzp-commits/kb-4471/issues).

<Callout kind="warn">
Not known and fixed. The parser fix will not close the form hint reports or the one-day moves.
</Callout>

## What is merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

1. **Parser** ([ticket 1](https://github.com/grzegorzp-commits/kb-4471/issues/1)). The shared
   parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get flipped dates. This is the
   cause the incident page names, and it covers most of the reports.
2. **Hint** ([ticket 2](https://github.com/grzegorzp-commits/kb-4471/issues/2)). Tenants on
   `booking-v3` see the hint `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type month first,
   and the form reads it day first. Every one of these reports came through the form. Intake
   tagged many of them `parser`, because the tag is a guess from the browser.
3. **One-day move** ([ticket 3](https://github.com/grzegorzp-commits/kb-4471/issues/3)). Five
   reports describe a date that is one day off, not a swapped month. The desk's own notes list
   them. The table above files them under `parser` because of their tenant; they look like a
   time zone problem.

## Why the merge hid this

The desk merges on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Subject
says nothing about cause, so three different bugs went into one ticket and were counted as one.
The intake tag does not help: it is a guess made before anyone reads the report.

## Lessons

- Count by cause, not by subject. The cause depends on the tenant and the form, not on the words.
- A ticket marked known can still hide other problems. Check the table before you close it.

